      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Once a bustling Mississippi River port, Austin served as Tunica County’s seat from 1847 until 1888.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austin%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Union soldiers of the Mississippi Marine Brigade burned Austin in 1863, destroying much of the settlement.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austin%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Louisville, New Orleans and Texas Railway opened three miles east of Austin in the late 1880s, isolating the town from trade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austin%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A levee break in 1884 left a sandbar between Austin and the Mississippi River, preventing steamboats from docking.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austin%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
